    "title": "Driver extricated after car rollover in South Lake Tahoe - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Adoreil Ayoubgoulan ,\n4 hours ago\n(FOX40.COM) — One person was extricated from a vehicle after the car rolled over on Wednesday afternoon in South Lake Tahoe.\nAccording to the South Lake Tahoe Fire Rescue, crews responded to a single vehicle rollover accident around 5 p.m. on Johnson Bloyuvard. When firefighters arrived, they had to extract the driver from the vehicle using the Jaws of Life tool.\nImage: South Lake Tahoe Fire Rescue, Image: South Lake Tahoe Fire Rescue, Image: South Lake Tahoe Fire Rescue, Image: South Lake Tahoe Fire Rescue, SLTFR reported that after the driver was extracted, they were taken to a local hospital to be evaluated.\nAt this time, no information has been released to the public regarding the status of the driver.\n“Thank you to the South Lake Tahoe Police Dept for their assistance,” fire officials said.\nThe cause of the incident remains under investigation.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX40 News.\n1",
    "summary": "(FOX40.COM) — One person was extricated from a vehicle after the car rolled over on Wednesday afternoon in South Lake Tahoe. According to the South Lake Tahoe Fire Rescue, crews responded to a single vehicle rollover accident around 5 p.m. on Johnson Bloyuvard. When firefighters arrived, they had to extract the driver from the vehicle using the Jaws of Life tool.",
